= Beat 14: THE AUTHENTICATION

INT. TOGG HILLS PANOPTICON — COLLECTION ROOM — NIGHT

The room has been cleared for the main event. The two hundred people are outside — held back by velvet and anticipation. Through the glass: Togg working the crowd, live on stream.

ELIZABETH stands alone at the center case with the authentication rig. A compact AI system — her design, her training data, her parameters. She's done this a hundred times.

She positions the optical scanner over the box. The system initializes.

On the monitors outside: Togg narrating to forty million viewers.

TOGG (ON MONITOR)
This is the moment. The verification
that backs everything. The AI system
that makes $GOAT the most credible
launch in the space.

The authentication system runs. Elizabeth watches the readouts.

Outside in the crowd, DEJA watches on a laptop. Her positions are loaded.

In the parking structure: Zach and Deja's car is gone. He's already clear.

The readout completes. Elizabeth studies it.

The Jordan card: authenticated. Stratospheric. The system assigns it a confidence score so high it's almost theoretical.

$GOAT HITS ITS LAUNCH PRICE. Then climbs. Then climbs faster.

On Deja's laptop, the short position triggers.

DEJA (V.O.)
(into earpiece, barely audible)
Positions pay.

Elizabeth is still looking at the readout.

She reads it again.

The authentication is clean. Her AI confirmed it. Her system. Her work.

She straightens. Looks at the box through the glass.

Her hand moves to her jacket pocket.

The loupe is there. Small. Old. Matching the one Zach still wears around his neck.

She looks at the box.

She knows this kind of work. She has spent years training a system to see it. But the system sees spectrophotometer tolerances and provenance documents. Not hands.

She presses the loupe to her eye.

She looks at the box.

For a very long time.
